Description: Stereo thumbnails at a scale that is not whole: each eye on the window's own pixels
 At 125 % (and every scale that is not whole) the icon view's stereo thumbnails showed a strip of each picture and the
 desktop behind the window through the rest of the cell. The cause was in the stereo layer (stereo-layer 1.18.1 fixes
 it for this version of Dolphin too); this patch makes Dolphin exact to the device pixel on top of it: the view, the
 information panel and the tooltip draw each eye on the layer's canvas, which is the window's own device pixels
 (Stereo::WidgetLayer::eyeCanvas(), eyeOffset(), setEyes()), the pictures kept in the view's eyes are read from the
 window's own pass, and a picture's hole is the pixels its pixmap is drawn on (at 125 % the pixmap has a whole number
 of device pixels, which is not its size in the window's pixels times the scale).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 576)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
